# Architecture Review Knowledge - Cursor Rules

## Project Context
This is an Obsidian Vault containing a structured knowledge base for architecture reviews.
The core data model consists of three node types:
- Success Criteria (sc-xxx) in `success_criteria/`
- Symptom (rf-xxx) in `symptom/`
- Root Cause (rc-xxx) in `root_cause/`

## Key Specifications
- Node Markdown format: see `miro-to-markdown/docs/backcasting-map-spec.md`
- Relationship field names (ADR-0004):
  - `triggers` / `triggered_by` — for RC→Symptom, Symptom→Symptom relationships
  - `threatens` / `threatened_by` — for Symptom→SC relationships
  - `leads_to` / `leads_from` — for RC→RC relationships (symmetric pair)
- Do NOT use deprecated names: `caused_by`, `triggers_symptoms`, `triggers_root_causes`, `explained_by`

## Conventions
- All node IDs must be unique
- `type` field is the source of truth for node type, NOT the `id` prefix
- Relationship references use Obsidian link format: `"[[rc-001]]"`
- YAML frontmatter keys require a space after `:`
- Empty lists use `key: []`, never `- []`

## Language
- Code, frontmatter keys, and technical terms: English
- Body content (Description, Context, Impact): Japanese or English depending on context

## Active Work
Current focus: `miro-to-markdown/` — building Backcasting MCP server and Miro integration.
See `miro-to-markdown/docs/prod-vision.md` for Epic vision.

